Now I have sufficient information to issue my verdict. Let me synthesize all findings.

**Key verification results:**
1. **Sonata (ICLR 2026)**: ✅ Confirmed real — paper exists, correctly described as using last-layer hidden representations via prefilling-stage adapter, achieves 20-60% thinking-token reduction on Qwen3 models, requires white-box access. Now properly cited and differentiated in Round 5.
2. **vLLM versions**: ✅ Confirmed — v0.19.0 (released April 2, 2026) and v0.20.1 (released ~May 3-4, 2026) are real. thinking_token_budget merged via PR #20859 on March 15, 2026. Paper correctly specifies SamplingParams (not extra_args).
3. **arXiv:2603.04444**: Minor concern resolved — this paper is "vLLM Semantic Router for Mixture-of-Modality Models" (cross-model routing), not thinking-budget specific. Differentiation from the proposed work is clear; no critical citation gap.
4. **New concurrent work found**: **arXiv:2505.11274 (SelfBudgeter, May 2026)** — uses the model itself to self-estimate required reasoning budget via budget-guided GRPO; achieves 61% compression on math tasks. This is directly concurrent work on per-request budget allocation but requires model fine-tuning (not black-box compatible). The reviewed paper does not cite this.

